    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "When we add a real number and an imaginary number, we get a complex number. The diagram shows where \\(2 + i\\) is in the complex number plane. What complex number is represented by point \\(A\\)?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Plot these complex numbers in the complex number plane and label them.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Diego says that all real numbers and all imaginary numbers are complex numbers but not all complex numbers are imaginary or real. Do you agree with Diego? Explain your reasoning.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A square root of a number \\(a\\) is a number whose square is \\(a\\). In other words, it is a solution to the equation \\(x^2 = a\\). Every positive real number has two real square roots. For example, look at the number 35. Its square roots are…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Similarly, every negative real number has two imaginary square roots. The two square roots of -1 are written \\(i\\) and \\(\\text- i\\). That means that",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle i^2 = \\text-1\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle (\\text- i)^2 = \\text-1\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Another example would be the number -17. Its square roots are \\(i\\sqrt{17}\\) and \\(\\text-i\\sqrt{17}\\), because",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle \\begin{array}{} \\left(i\\sqrt{17}\\right)^2 &= 17i^2 \\\\ &=\\text-17 \\end{array}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-022",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\displaystyle \\begin{array}{} \\left(\\text-i\\sqrt{17}\\right)^2 &=17(\\text-i)^2 \\\\ &= 17i^2 \\\\ & =\\text-17 \\end{array}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-023",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "In general, if \\(a\\) is a positive real number, then the square roots of \\(\\text- a\\) are \\(i \\sqrt{a}\\) and \\(\\text- i \\sqrt{a}\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-024",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Rarely, we might see something like \\(\\sqrt{\\text-17}\\). It’s not immediately clear which of the two square roots it is supposed to represent. By convention, \\(\\sqrt{\\text-17}\\) is defined to indicate the square root on the positive…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-025",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "When we add a real number and an imaginary number, we get a complex number. Together, the real number line and the imaginary number line form a coordinate system that can be used to represent any complex number as a point in the complex…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-026",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "In this context, people call the real number line the real axis and the imaginary number line the imaginary axis. This is different than the coordinate plane you have seen before because those points were pairs of real numbers, like…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-027",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A number in the complex plane. It can be written as \\(a + bi\\), where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are real numbers and \\(i^2 = \\text-1\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L11-ACTIVITY-028",
      "SourceSection": "11.4: Complex Numbers",
      "SourceExcerpt": "A number on the imaginary number line. It can be written as \\(bi\\), where \\(b\\) is a real number and \\(i^2 = \\text-1\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
